  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (RNA, multi-profile, PCA n2000, avgpool) is the current best at 0.591 acc, substantially outperforming single-profile RNA (0.485) and image-only ResNet50 (0.208). Avgpool clearly beats transformer for RNA aggregation (0.591 vs 0.519). The key remaining uncertainty within the RNA pipeline is whether the linear PCA representation is a bottleneck or already near-optimal. Question: config_005 changes only the RNA encoder from PCA to scvi_n200 while holding the proven-best multi-profile + avgpool setting fixed, giving a clean single-variable comparison against config_002. Why best next: it isolates the representation effect without introducing confounds from fusion or image modality; if scvi improves on PCA, it signals that learned cell-relationship encodings matter and justifies further encoder exploration; if it does not, it confirms PCA is sufficient and redirects budget toward multimodal fusion or better image encoders. This is the highest-information-per-experiment choice given the limited budget."
